10. INTERVIEW QUESTIONS

Q1. What is pip list?

It displays installed Python packages and their versions in a readable table.

Q2. What is pip freeze?

It displays installed distributions in requirements-file format.

Q3. Why do developers use pip freeze?

To capture installed package versions and help recreate an environment.

Q4. Does pip freeze show only packages imported in our code?

No. It generally lists installed distributions, including transitive dependencies.

Q5. How do you install packages from requirements.txt?

python -m pip install -r requirements.txt

Q6. What is a virtual environment?

An isolated Python environment that keeps project dependencies separate.

Q7. Can two Django projects use different Django versions?

Yes, when each project has its own virtual environment.

Q8. What is the difference between pip freeze and pip list --format=freeze?

Both can display package versions in requirements-style output. Their purposes and command interfaces differ, but their outputs are similar.

Q9. What is pip check?

It checks whether installed packages have compatible dependencies.

python -m pip check

Q10. Is pip freeze a complete production lockfile?

No. It is a snapshot of installed distributions. Production dependencies should be reviewed, tested and managed carefully.

